(text "J1: fused battery logic branch only. D1 band = K -> VB_LOGIC.\nMotor power and Pi USB-C stay off this board.\nJ2: 1 E5V CN7-6 / 2 GND / 3 NUCLEO 3V3 CN6-4." (at 20.32 82.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a9ace709-c849-400c-85fd-d59d60d2347d"))
(text "R1/R2 = 100k/22k. Vadc = VB_LOGIC x 22/122.\nJP1 OPEN for first power-up. J10.1 -> PA4 (CN8-3).\nBAT_DIV and BAT_ADC connect ONLY through JP1." (at 20.32 149.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "dd2587ef-1b2f-4d93-895a-82161755dbc2"))
(text "L: PA6/PA7 (CN5-5/4). R: PA0/PA1 (CN8-1/2).\nMotor pigtail: BLUE=3V3, BLACK=GND, YELLOW=A, GREEN=B.\nRED/WHITE -> MDD power outputs; never join WHITE to GND." (at 20.32 245.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8c57936b-bbc7-450e-9105-59b7ee9a1ce6"))
(text "J6: PA8/9/10/11 -> M1A/B, M2A/B, 5=GND.\nJ7 = MDD3A header order M1A/M1B/5VO/GND/M2A/M2B, 1:1 harness.\nJ7.3 = NC: MDD3A 5VO is never connected (leave cavity empty).\nR7-10 hold inputs LOW (brake) while the MCU is in reset.\nCable removal also removes pull-downs." (at 190.5 245.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d58a212b-239e-4ad1-9c83-012ef0dc7a70"))
(text "J8.2 PB6 TX -> J9.3 -> Pi pin10 RX\nJ8.3 PB7 RX <- J9.2 <- Pi pin8 TX\nJ8.1/J9.1 GND -> Pi pin6. No Pi power.\nJ9 order = Pi pins 6/8/10, 1:1 3-pin harness." (at 330.2 220.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8fc79e1f-f4bc-4fd9-938c-574e70dc795f"))
(text "J12: GND / PB13 SCK / PB14 MISO / PB15 MOSI / PB12 CS / PB0 INT1.\nJ11 module order: VCC, GND, AD0/MISO, SDA/MOSI, SCL/SCLK, CS, INT1.\nJP2 CLOSED (jumper cap): NUCLEO 3V3 -> module VCC (module has its own LDO).\nRemove the cap only to isolate the module. Never feed 5V to sensor I/O.\nAuxiliary module 3V3 / NC / INT2 are not connected here." (at 193.04 130.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "30539b22-5fcb-4ace-8d5d-794c9f1652c0"))
(text "90 x 70 mm PERFBOARD - Rev B / 2026-09-22\nAll board pads on 2.54 mm grid. JST XH (2.50 mm, <=6 pins) headers solder directly; dry-fit first. No PH on this board.\nUser.1/User.2 are insulated hand wires, not manufactured copper. Use WIRING.csv.\nICM module: male header into the J11 socket, component side up, body toward the board edge." (at 20.32 269.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "dbb46726-06ef-4f11-9418-d39e9e105caa"))
